  <running_head>Admonitio.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">imbibi, &amp; illam solam, &amp; uni-</l>
    <l n="2">cam, (vel &amp; solitariam) esse</l>
    <l n="3">Rationem ; atque ut me docuit</l>
    <l n="4">Paulus Sarpius, illum quem at-</l>
    <l n="5">trecto corporis Romanensis mor-</l>
    <l n="6">bum, esse <i>noli me tangere</i>, qui vel</l>
    <l n="7">primoribus digitis tactus, vitam</l>
    <l n="8">&amp; Papæ &amp; toti Romanensi ap-</l>
    <l n="9">paratui auferre debeat , que-</l>
    <l n="10">madmodum doceo capite deci-</l>
    <l n="11">mo tertio hujus opellæ.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Nec finis est aliquid deside-</l>
    <l n="13">randi in nova nostra Ratione ;</l>
    <l n="14">nam, non ita pridem Vir emunctæ</l>
    <l n="15">naris &amp; qui per omnia com-</l>
    <l n="16">mendat &amp; laudat novam nostram</l>
    <l n="17">Rationem, affirmat illam quam</l>
    <l n="18">retego veritatem , de illarum</l>
    <l n="19">esse numero quæ profundè de-</l>
    <l n="20">mersæ in puteo Democriti, nun-</l>
    <l n="21">quam inde eximentur , ut lu-</l>
    <l n="22">cem conspiciant ; Papam securum</l>
    <l n="23">esse ruinæ quæ impendeat</l>
    <l n="24">suo</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "suo" at foot right is the start of the next page's first word; treated as catchword. Greek or Latin letters all Latin. Some ink spots on the scan (ignored).</notes>
